course: dictionary
lesson: 15009
title: Left-over words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Residual is a formal word for what is left over after most of something has gone or been used. «There was only a residual amount of juice in the bottle.» Most of the juice has been poured out, and a small amount remains.
explain: Think of residual as a remainder. «After we shared the cake, a residual crumb sat on the plate.» The crumb is what is left once everyone has had a piece.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «The oven was switched off, but the residual heat kept the kitchen warm.» The oven is off, yet warmth is still there, so residual heat means heat that is left over. Check by swapping in "left over": it still makes sense.
fact: Residual means left over after most of something has gone or been used.
fact: Residual is a formal word, so you will meet it in science, maths and exams.
fact: In maths and science, a residual can be the amount left over, or the difference between a real value and a predicted one.
fact: Phrases you may see are residual heat, residual amount and residual value.
fact: As a noun, residuals (plural) can mean money paid to actors when a show is shown again.
exercise: «Only a residual amount of paint was left in the tin.» What does residual mean here? | *Left over | Spilled on the floor | Brand new | Very heavy
exercise: «The pan was still warm from the residual heat of the stove.» What is residual heat? | *Heat left over after the stove was switched off | A special kind of pan | Heat from a fire that has just been lit | Cold air blowing from a fan
exercise: Which word means the same as residual? | Empty | *Remaining | Sudden | Sharp
test: «After the test, a residual feeling of worry stayed with Sam.» What does residual mean here? | Very loud | *Left over after most of it had gone | Brand new | Happy and free
test: In maths, Ava finds the difference between a real value and a predicted one. What is this difference called? | Its total | Its zero | *Its residual | Its shape
exam: In the phrase «residual water in the jug», which word is closest in meaning to residual? | *Left over | Clean | Frozen | Boiling
